  "slug": "server-web-88a4",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and publications deliver specialized sequence, structure, and omics analyses through user-facing web and R interfaces.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is delivery of specialized analyses as accessible, user-facing tools. GNAT searches microbial and viral databases for protein homologues and clusters their genomic neighbourhoods into an interactive web interface. RNApdbee 3.0 is a web server that annotates RNA secondary structure from 3D coordinates, classifying base pairs and interactions and exporting dot-bracket notation. phylobar, an R package, links interactive stacked barplots to taxonomic or cell-type hierarchies to expose multiresolution composition in omics data. PGAP2, the only published item here, is an open toolkit for prokaryotic pan-genome analysis built on fine-grained feature networks, with improved ortholog identification. What is new is the integration of classification, annotation, and visualization within interactive or reproducible interfaces. Three of the four are preprints, and their summaries describe function rather than comparative benchmarks.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-11"
}
